      "content": "8.1 Ancient India"
    },
    {
      "id": "bxk4rx5",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Indus Valley Civilization (3300–1300 BCE)"
    },
    {
      "id": "ggo3dxr",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Major sites: Harappa (Punjab, Pakistan), Mohenjo-daro (Sindh, Pakistan), Lothal (Gujarat), Dholavira (Gujarat), Kalibangan (Rajasthan), Rakhigarhi (Haryana)",
        "Town planning: Grid system, drainage, granaries, public baths",
        "No evidence of temples; Mother Goddess worship; Pashupati seal",
        "Declined around 1900 BCE; causes debated (Aryan invasion theory vs. climate change/river drying)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "sk63vz6",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Vedic Age"
    },
    {
      "id": "cjbup8z",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Early Vedic (1500–1000 BCE): Rigveda; pastoral, nomadic; Iran/Afghanistan origin",
        "Later Vedic (1000–600 BCE): Iron Age; settled agriculture; social stratification; Upanishads",
        "Four Vedas: Rigveda (hymns), Samaveda (melodies), Yajurveda (rituals), Atharvaveda (spells)"
      ]
    },
    {
